    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Outbound send errors by reason",
      "id": 7,
      "description": "Per-second rate of outbound sends that failed, split by reason. `full` means the shared instruction channel was saturated and the message was dropped outright — nothing resends it. `closed` means the network task has shut down, which is a different problem entirely. Both are lagging indicators: by the time this moves, messages have already been lost. The saturation panel in the transport-layer row is the leading one.",
