    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Instruction queue depth vs capacity (two samplers)",
      "id": 15,
      "description": "Depth of the shared p2p instruction channel against its capacity, from two independent samplers. `at dequeue` is sop2p's own reading, taken inside the network task each time it dequeues an instruction — so it only moves while that task is draining, and holds its last value once the network goes idle. `sender-side poll` is read every 5s from outside the network task, so it keeps reporting regardless of whether that task is making progress. The two agreeing is normal; the interesting case is disagreement. The sender-side line climbing while the dequeue line goes flat means the network task has stopped draining, which is the failure the sender-side sample exists to catch. Sends use try_send, so a depth at capacity means outbound messages are being dropped.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 57
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "fillOpacity": 10
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom"
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "expr": "sop2p_instruction_queue_depth_current{instance=~\"$instance\"}",
          "legendFormat": "{{instance}} depth (at dequeue)",
          "refId": "A"
        },
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "expr": "supra_network_instruction_queue_depth_current{instance=~\"$instance\"}",
          "legendFormat": "{{instance}} depth (sender-side poll)",
          "refId": "B"
        },
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "expr": "sop2p_instruction_queue_capacity_current{instance=~\"$instance\"}",
          "legendFormat": "{{instance}} capacity",
          "refId": "C"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Instruction queue saturation",
      "id": 16,
      "description": "Sender-side queue depth as a fraction of capacity: how close the shared p2p instruction channel is to dropping outbound messages. This is the leading indicator — sends use try_send, so at 100% the next send is discarded and only `network.send_errors` {reason=\"full\"} will show it, after the fact. The channel is shared by consensus, mempool, the epoch manager, the commitment signer and the DKG, so a rising ratio is not necessarily any one service's doing; compare against the inbound-by-service panels to see whose traffic is behind it. Alert on this with a `for:` duration rather than on a single scrape.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 57
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "percentunit",
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "fillOpacity": 10
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom"
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
